<title>UK: British summer time ends on October 27.</title>
<headline>British summer time ends on October 27.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British &quot;summer time&quot; ends at two a.m. on October 27 when clocks in Britain are put back one hour to one a.m. (0100 GMT).</p>
<p>In 1997, the summer time period will run from March 30 to October 26.</p>
</text>
